00:01:54.208 --> 00:01:56.748
- The importance of salary
negotiation is really

00:01:56.748 --> 00:01:58.538
underestimated by most people.

00:01:58.538 --> 00:02:01.106
In this video we're going
to show you exactly why

00:02:01.106 --> 00:02:05.308
it is so important to consistently
negotiate your salary.

00:02:05.308 --> 00:02:08.779
First of all, it really matters
for your lifetime earnings.

00:02:08.779 --> 00:02:10.608
It makes a huge difference.

00:02:10.608 --> 00:02:11.777
And research has shown

00:02:11.777 --> 00:02:15.428
that people who consistently
negotiate their salary

00:02:15.428 --> 00:02:17.058
over their entire lifetime

00:02:17.058 --> 00:02:21.048
earn about $1 million more
throughout their entire career.

00:02:21.048 --> 00:02:24.348
Let's start with getting more.

00:02:24.348 --> 00:02:26.866
I want to show you a
simple theoretical graph

00:02:26.866 --> 00:02:31.198
that illustrates how
salary negotiations really

00:02:31.198 --> 00:02:34.158
impact your salary and how
it increases your earnings

00:02:34.158 --> 00:02:36.018
over your entire lifetime.

00:02:36.018 --> 00:02:37.178
In this case example

00:02:37.178 --> 00:02:39.548
we have two fictional people, Christian

00:02:39.548 --> 00:02:41.538
who does not negotiate a salary.

00:02:41.538 --> 00:02:44.948
So for him, I assumed
a 1% increase basically

00:02:44.948 --> 00:02:47.398
in line with inflation over each year.

00:02:47.398 --> 00:02:48.984
On the other hand, there's Theodor

00:02:48.984 --> 00:02:51.984
he negotiates his salary every three years

00:02:51.984 --> 00:02:56.288
and he is she a 5% average
negotiation success

00:02:56.288 --> 00:02:58.688
which is really in line
with what you can expect.

00:02:58.688 --> 00:03:00.148
By the end of his career,

00:03:00.148 --> 00:03:03.362
Theodore will earn about
$140,000 each year.

00:03:03.362 --> 00:03:06.578
While Christian will be
stuck at roughly 80,000.

00:03:06.578 --> 00:03:09.378
So this is already a huge difference.

00:03:09.378 --> 00:03:12.558
If you add up all the years
where Theodore earns more

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:14.678
and more money than Christian

00:03:14.678 --> 00:03:19.058
throughout that entire career,
the difference is enormous.

00:03:19.058 --> 00:03:22.521
In this case example,
it's about $1.2 million.

00:03:23.368 --> 00:03:25.868
I've oversimplified this, obviously,

00:03:25.868 --> 00:03:29.048
but it really proves the
point how important it is

00:03:29.048 --> 00:03:31.798
to not be afraid of negotiating a salary.

00:03:31.798 --> 00:03:34.091
Usually your employer
will respect you more

00:03:34.091 --> 00:03:36.611
If you ask what you are worth.

00:03:38.498 --> 00:03:41.418
- So the one thing is to
freshly negotiate your salary

00:03:41.418 --> 00:03:43.088
once you get a new job.

00:03:43.088 --> 00:03:45.808
But the other thing is once
you're already in the job

00:03:45.808 --> 00:03:49.268
then also to be able to
negotiate regular raises.

00:03:49.268 --> 00:03:51.688
And this is the topic
that we are going to talk

00:03:51.688 --> 00:03:53.268
about in this section.

00:03:53.268 --> 00:03:54.858
In this first lecture

00:03:54.858 --> 00:03:57.218
I wanna talk about what is realistic?

00:03:57.218 --> 00:03:58.952
What can you ask for a raise?

00:03:58.952 --> 00:04:02.358
Because this is indeed the
question that I get most

00:04:02.358 --> 00:04:04.608
frequently when I discuss this topic

00:04:04.608 --> 00:04:05.958
with friends and colleagues.

00:04:05.958 --> 00:04:07.008
and hear it all from the head

00:04:07.008 --> 00:04:08.818
So really help you with some data.

00:04:08.818 --> 00:04:11.448
So in this lecture, I want to help you

00:04:11.448 --> 00:04:13.494
by providing a little orientation,

00:04:13.494 --> 00:04:16.308
some points of data that might help you

00:04:16.308 --> 00:04:17.748
to guide this discussion.

00:04:17.748 --> 00:04:20.248
And the first thing to
be aware of is of course

00:04:20.248 --> 00:04:23.798
the inflation rate measured
by the consumer price index.

00:04:23.798 --> 00:04:26.438
This measures how much prices increase

00:04:26.438 --> 00:04:29.278
on average for the
consumer every single year.

00:04:29.278 --> 00:04:30.668
Of course these venues differ

00:04:30.668 --> 00:04:32.241
significantly country by country.

00:04:32.241 --> 00:04:35.188
So you should take this
into consideration depending

00:04:35.188 --> 00:04:36.988
on your geography that you work in.

00:04:36.988 --> 00:04:38.578
So putting some data for Germany

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:41.128
you can see here that the
values pretty much fluctuate

00:04:41.128 --> 00:04:43.358
between one and 2% per year.

00:04:43.358 --> 00:04:44.988
And this is exactly the average

00:04:44.988 --> 00:04:47.648
that you can expect for
most developed countries.

00:04:47.648 --> 00:04:51.588
So one to 2% per year, annual
consumer price inflation.

00:04:51.588 --> 00:04:54.152
So make sure to research
this value for your country.

00:04:54.152 --> 00:04:57.128
The index might be called a bit different

00:04:57.128 --> 00:04:59.658
there might be different
indices, measuring concepts

00:04:59.658 --> 00:05:01.538
like this as well for your country.

00:05:01.538 --> 00:05:02.371
So look it up in a second.

00:05:02.371 --> 00:05:04.758
Similar index that might be helpful here

00:05:04.758 --> 00:05:06.848
is the labor cost index.

00:05:06.848 --> 00:05:08.686
The choice you'll have much on average

00:05:08.686 --> 00:05:10.238
the price for labor.

00:05:10.238 --> 00:05:13.658
So the salaries in the country
have gone up over time.

00:05:13.658 --> 00:05:15.538
And often these values are more

00:05:15.538 --> 00:05:17.198
or less similar in some countries.

00:05:17.198 --> 00:05:19.798
The one might be higher than
the other, but here again

00:05:19.798 --> 00:05:23.276
if on average salaries
go up by 2% every year

00:05:23.276 --> 00:05:25.824
this is where it can give
you a certain indication

00:05:25.824 --> 00:05:27.508
of what you should target.

00:05:27.508 --> 00:05:30.038
Then, of course you
should not really be happy

00:05:30.038 --> 00:05:33.568
with just getting a salary
on the level of inflation.

00:05:33.568 --> 00:05:36.275
Because if you exactly
meet the inflation number

00:05:36.275 --> 00:05:38.948
you do not really have a salary increase.

00:05:38.948 --> 00:05:41.338
And just the fact that
now you can buy next year

00:05:41.338 --> 00:05:44.608
as much things with
your money as last year.

00:05:44.608 --> 00:05:45.441
Or to put it differently,

00:05:45.441 --> 00:05:47.968
If you're not even managed
to get a salary raise

00:05:47.968 --> 00:05:50.848
that meets inflation, you
will lose purchasing power.

00:05:50.848 --> 00:05:54.108
You pretty much lose value
off your money year on year.

00:05:54.108 --> 00:05:56.565
And for these reasons,
compensation for inflation

00:05:56.565 --> 00:05:58.808
should pretty much be the minimum

00:05:58.808 --> 00:06:01.478
the minimum amount that you ask for

00:06:01.478 --> 00:06:04.848
and that you get when you
go into these conversations.

00:06:04.848 --> 00:06:06.968
So if this is the one end of the spectrum,

00:06:06.968 --> 00:06:09.548
then what is the other
end of the spectrum?

00:06:09.548 --> 00:06:11.968
And just to give you
a ballpark figure here

00:06:11.968 --> 00:06:14.721
one number that you can expect to receive

00:06:14.721 --> 00:06:19.058
if you work in a so-called
accelerated career environment

00:06:19.058 --> 00:06:22.878
such as consulting or
banking, is roughly an average

00:06:22.878 --> 00:06:25.738
of a salary increase of 10% per year.

00:06:25.738 --> 00:06:29.058
So I'd argue that there are
only very very few careers,

00:06:29.058 --> 00:06:31.098
very, very few roads that you can get

00:06:31.098 --> 00:06:33.548
a longterm average salary increase

00:06:33.548 --> 00:06:35.825
of more than 10% per year.

00:06:35.825 --> 00:06:40.008
So aim for this 10% in
these very high pace

00:06:40.008 --> 00:06:41.838
accelerated career environments.

00:06:41.838 --> 00:06:42.938
Of course, there's a reason

00:06:42.938 --> 00:06:45.108
that these people get this type of money

00:06:45.108 --> 00:06:47.388
of course and these jobs
often need to work a lot.

00:06:47.388 --> 00:06:50.143
The performance pressure on
you is quite significant.

00:06:50.143 --> 00:06:52.768
So if you are out in a more generous stand

00:06:52.768 --> 00:06:55.108
at nine to five corporate job,

00:06:55.108 --> 00:06:57.245
probably this is a battalion
should be then adjusted

00:06:57.245 --> 00:06:59.208
to a bit of a lower number.

00:06:59.208 --> 00:07:02.448
So one to 2%, this is the
minimum that you should get.

00:07:02.448 --> 00:07:04.523
This is all such what
some companies provide

00:07:04.523 --> 00:07:08.258
just by themselves as a
yearly inflation compensation

00:07:08.258 --> 00:07:09.208
to the employees.

00:07:09.208 --> 00:07:10.525
And then on top of that you should to ask

00:07:10.525 --> 00:07:12.828
for an increase that is up to 10%

00:07:12.828 --> 00:07:14.778
based on the type of
career that you're in.

00:07:14.778 --> 00:07:16.938
And of course here, the
importance is also to see this

00:07:16.938 --> 00:07:18.218
as a longterm average.

00:07:18.218 --> 00:07:20.608
So it's absolutely okay to maybe one year

00:07:20.608 --> 00:07:22.388
not get that much of a raise.

00:07:22.388 --> 00:07:24.988
If then after two years
or after three years,

00:07:24.988 --> 00:07:27.358
you get an even higher salary increase

00:07:27.358 --> 00:07:29.748
maybe if you step up to
the next higher position.

00:07:29.748 --> 00:07:31.438
But make sure that on average,

00:07:31.438 --> 00:07:33.588
these are the targets
that you can achieve.

00:07:35.898 --> 00:07:37.028
- Welcome to this section

00:07:37.028 --> 00:07:39.288
in which we will talk
about how to increase

00:07:39.288 --> 00:07:42.287
the overall value for
both sides on the table.

00:07:42.287 --> 00:07:46.498
This concept is called value
creation and negotiations.

00:07:46.498 --> 00:07:48.615
And it's a very important concept

00:07:48.615 --> 00:07:52.048
that you can also apply
to salary negotiations.

00:07:52.048 --> 00:07:55.938
So far we've really simplified
the salary negotiation

00:07:55.938 --> 00:08:00.938
and only talked about your
total compensation as $1 figure.

00:08:01.045 --> 00:08:04.008
But actually there are many
many different elements

00:08:04.008 --> 00:08:06.078
that make up your total compensation

00:08:06.078 --> 00:08:07.738
and you can make leverage use

00:08:07.738 --> 00:08:10.658
of these different
elements to create value

00:08:10.658 --> 00:08:12.098
in the negotiation.

00:08:12.098 --> 00:08:13.578
It is really a common trap

00:08:13.578 --> 00:08:16.948
or mistake people make
in salary negotiations

00:08:16.948 --> 00:08:20.078
because they simplify the
many different elements

00:08:20.078 --> 00:08:22.795
into $1 figure and this
way they go heads on

00:08:22.795 --> 00:08:24.988
with their employer instead
of thinking about clever

00:08:24.988 --> 00:08:28.298
and nuanced ways to create value.

00:08:28.298 --> 00:08:30.008
The key insight here is the following.

00:08:30.008 --> 00:08:31.918
You should aim to negotiate

00:08:31.918 --> 00:08:35.458
for salary components
that are worth more to you

00:08:35.458 --> 00:08:37.306
and worth less to your employer.

00:08:37.306 --> 00:08:40.477
By this way you can
basically create value.

00:08:40.477 --> 00:08:42.648
This will enable you to grow

00:08:42.648 --> 00:08:45.618
your total compensation by a lot.

00:08:45.618 --> 00:08:48.418
Your employer might be bound
by certain salary bands

00:08:48.418 --> 00:08:51.018
that are very specific to your role.

00:08:51.018 --> 00:08:53.788
And maybe you just barely
missed the qualification

00:08:53.788 --> 00:08:54.968
for a more senior role

00:08:54.968 --> 00:08:58.378
and it would also have a
different salary range of course.

00:08:58.378 --> 00:09:00.238
In this case you can try to negotiate

00:09:00.238 --> 00:09:01.478
for a much faster review

00:09:01.478 --> 00:09:03.738
of your current role and your promotion.

00:09:03.738 --> 00:09:06.838
This gives you a much faster
runway to the next promotion

00:09:06.838 --> 00:09:09.808
and therefore a much faster
access to a higher salary.

00:09:09.808 --> 00:09:11.908
Another example would be maybe you want

00:09:11.908 --> 00:09:13.818
a different job title because you know

00:09:13.818 --> 00:09:15.348
that if you switch jobs

00:09:15.348 --> 00:09:17.899
it will give you a much
better salary range.

00:09:17.899 --> 00:09:21.078
This will actually cost your
current employer nothing.

00:09:21.078 --> 00:09:23.888
If they can defend it against
other employees, of course.

00:09:23.888 --> 00:09:26.178
But it could be worth a lot to you.

00:09:26.178 --> 00:09:29.238
To give you some ideas
of salary components

00:09:29.238 --> 00:09:31.435
that you can negotiate
for and that other people

00:09:31.435 --> 00:09:35.928
have negotiated for, I will
now show you a brief overview.

00:09:35.928 --> 00:09:38.128
Besides the overall component, of course,

00:09:38.128 --> 00:09:40.768
your annual cash compensation,

00:09:40.768 --> 00:09:42.868
you can negotiate for vacation days.

00:09:42.868 --> 00:09:45.608
You can negotiate for a sign on bonus

00:09:45.608 --> 00:09:48.248
in case you are switching
to a new employer.

00:09:48.248 --> 00:09:50.483
Other common types of
compensation components

00:09:50.483 --> 00:09:53.538
can be your relocation coverage.

00:09:53.538 --> 00:09:57.018
It could be a tuition
allowance, your job title

00:09:57.018 --> 00:09:59.708
as we discussed in the previous example.

00:09:59.708 --> 00:10:01.718
It could be the early review.

00:10:01.718 --> 00:10:05.208
It could be a company card
or maybe a mobility budget

00:10:05.208 --> 00:10:09.111
or in case of particular
smaller companies or startups,

00:10:09.111 --> 00:10:11.588
maybe you can negotiate for a visa package

00:10:11.588 --> 00:10:13.588
or an equity option package

00:10:13.588 --> 00:10:16.668
that gives you a really strong
incentive in the long run

00:10:16.668 --> 00:10:17.788
to stay with the company

00:10:17.788 --> 00:10:20.238
which is also of course,
interesting to your employer.

00:10:20.238 --> 00:10:23.708
You can really extend this
list to many other elements.

00:10:23.708 --> 00:10:25.948
I've shown some here on this slide.

00:10:25.948 --> 00:10:29.128
Maybe if you already
are a father or a mother

00:10:29.128 --> 00:10:32.615
you can negotiate for childcare
support, a parental leave,

00:10:32.615 --> 00:10:36.418
or maybe for other people
awareness or fitness program.

00:10:36.418 --> 00:10:38.058
Just look through all the components

00:10:38.058 --> 00:10:41.348
I'm showing you here on
this slide and get creative.

00:10:41.348 --> 00:10:44.758
You will find that by
opening new opportunities

00:10:44.758 --> 00:10:48.128
for your employer to compensate
you in some sort of way

00:10:48.128 --> 00:10:51.436
be it money monetary or
in case of job titles

00:10:51.436 --> 00:10:54.728
giving you future possibilities
and future options,

00:10:54.728 --> 00:10:57.561
you can really create a lot of value

00:10:57.561 --> 00:10:59.828
for yourself in the negotiation.

00:10:59.828 --> 00:11:02.216
As you're preparing for
your next negotiation,

00:11:02.216 --> 00:11:05.208
write down the different salary components

00:11:05.208 --> 00:11:08.384
that would be relevant
for your negotiation now.

